# Paths Docker leaves out of the build context, the files it sends to the
# image build. build/ict/Dockerfile copies only sources, so leave out the rest.
# A checkout where ICT has run holds large build trees (cache/, workspace/,
# webui-workspace/), often owned by root: sending them would slow every image
# build, and an unreadable file would fail it.
.git
.github
.vscode
# local binaries; build/ict/ holds the Dockerfile
build
!build/ict
builds
downloads
benchmark-logs
cache
tmp
workspace
webui-workspace
.ai-cache
dist
*.log
/image-composer-tool
/live-installer
web/node_modules
web/dist
image-templates/.ict-adv-*.yml
